# WooCommerce Integration

Commerce is a **swappable capability** — not every project has it. Check
`PROJECT.md` before assuming WooCommerce is present.

## Keep it removable

Commerce code must be deletable as a group. That means:

- Classes in `lib/class-woocommerce*.php` and commerce-named siblings, all
  instantiated from a single `define_woocommerce_hooks()` entry point
- Functions in `includes/woocommerce/`, loaded from
  `includes/woocommerce/bootstrap.php` (one require in `includes/init.php`)
- REST endpoints in `public/class-api-*.php`, each gating itself through
  `Api::is_available()` and listed in `Init::define_api_hooks()` — where the
  `class_exists()` test means deleting the file is enough
- Styles in capability-named Sass directories, each with one import line
- **Nothing commerce-specific at the root of `includes/`** — root files are always
  loaded and can never be deleted. A commerce predicate placed there permanently
  welds commerce into the starter. This happened once already: 12 commerce
  functions sat in `includes/helper-functions.php` until 2026-08-17.

`Skaflow\WooCommerce` in `lib/class-woocommerce.php` is that single entry point.
It guards on the plugin, then constructs every commerce class:

```php
// lib/class-woocommerce.php
public function __construct() {
	if ( ! class_exists( 'WooCommerce' ) ) {
		return;
	}
	new WooCommerce_Admin();
	// ...one line per commerce class
}
```

`Init::define_woocommerce_hooks()` does nothing but `new WooCommerce()`, so the
guard covers all of them. Do not instantiate a commerce class anywhere else.

Block registration is directory-driven and does **not** check for WooCommerce, so
commerce blocks will register on a site without it. Guard inside `render.php` or
record the dependency for the strip manifest.

`woocommerce/` holds **template overrides only**. Never put hooks or classes
there.

## ACF vs native admin UI

| Situation | Approach |
|---|---|
| Field on `product`, standard edit screen | ACF JSON in `acf-json/` |
| Field on `product_variation` or in the Variations panel | **Native WC hooks** |
| Meta shown in Product data tabs | Native WC hooks + WC UI components |
| Legacy storage format from a previous plugin | Same meta key; normalise on save only |

### `product_variation` has no edit screen

It is registered with `show_ui: false` — variations are edited inside the parent
product's **Variations** tab, loaded over AJAX. ACF has no screen to render on, so
a `post_type == product_variation` location rule silently does nothing.

Use the bridge pattern instead:

| Step | Hook |
|---|---|
| Render | `woocommerce_variation_options` |
| Save | `woocommerce_save_product_variation` |
| Admin JS re-init | `woocommerce_variations_loaded` |

Variation fields POST as arrays keyed by variation ID. **If the POST key is
absent entirely, do not delete existing meta** — an absent key means the panel
wasn't loaded, not that the value was cleared.

## Legacy meta keys are contracts

When rebuilding over an existing store, meta keys and their storage formats are
data contracts. Never rename a key without an approved migration; hold each one
in a private class constant so the string appears once. Normalise format on save
if needed, but read what is already there.

Project-specific keys and formats live in the matching `project-*-meta` rule, not
here.

## Admin assets

WooCommerce product screens do not load `build/index.css`. Small wp-admin UI may
enqueue static files from `assets/js/` and `assets/css/` with `filemtime()`
versioning, on `admin_enqueue_scripts`, restricted to product edit screens.
Frontend shop styles go through the Sass build.

## Frontend

Grid and card interactions must be delegated — product grids are re-populated by
Load More and filters. See `.cursor/rules/sf-event-delegation.mdc`.

For WooCommerce's own markup where no class can be injected, style the plugin's
selector directly with a Sass mixin rather than overriding templates. See
`.cursor/rules/sf-sass-architecture.mdc`.

## Verification for any admin field change

1. **CLI** — read the meta before and after on a record with known data.
2. **wp-admin** — open that record, confirm display, edit, save, and that sibling
   meta is unchanged.

```bash
ddev wp post meta get <id> <key> --format=json
```

## Anti-patterns

- ACF on `product_variation` expecting wp-admin visibility
- Renaming legacy meta keys without a migration
- Hooks or classes inside `woocommerce/`
- Standalone functions outside the `Skaflow\` namespace for stateful features
- Commerce helpers in `includes/helper-functions.php`
- Deleting variation meta when the POST key is entirely absent
- Bulk data migration for schema-only work

